.TH XDG\-DESKTOP\-PORTAL\-XEONDESKTOP 8 2026-10-26 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xdg\-desktop\-portal\-xeondesktop \- XeonDesktop's Open and Save As dialogs for xdg\-desktop\-portal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY /usr/lib/xdg\-desktop\-portal\-xeondesktop
.RB [ \-\-replace ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xdg\-desktop\-portal\-xeondesktop
is a backend of
.BR xdg\-desktop\-portal (1).
It serves the
.B org.freedesktop.impl.portal.FileChooser
interface on the session bus, as
.BR org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.xeondesktop ,
so that programs asking the portal for a file get XeonDesktop's own Open
and Save As dialogs: Flatpak programs, GTK\~4 programs, Firefox and
Chromium, and GTK\~3 programs' native file choosers.
It is started by D\-Bus activation when
.B xdg\-desktop\-portal
first needs it; there is no need to run it by hand.
.PP
The dialogs are laid out as Windows XP's (Look in, the Places bar, File
name and Files of type) in every display style, which gives them their
colours and controls, with Windows\~7's search box for the folder shown.
Folder pickers are the same dialog, listing folders only.
The list is the folder view of
.BR xd\-files (1).
Typing a folder's path in File name goes there, typing a pattern such as
.B *.txt
shows only the files matching it, and Save As adds the file type's
extension to a name without one, as Windows did.
.PP
A XeonDesktop session uses it through
.IR /usr/share/xdg\-desktop\-portal/xeondesktop\-portals.conf ,
and the compositor
.RB ( xd\-compositor (1))
sets
.B GTK_USE_PORTAL=1
and adds
.B portals
to
.B GDK_DEBUG
so that GTK programs ask the portal.
Plain GTK\~3 file chooser dialogs (GtkFileChooserDialog) stay GTK's own.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-replace
Take over the bus name from another instance.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/xdg\-desktop\-portal/portals/xeondesktop.portal
Tells
.B xdg\-desktop\-portal
which interfaces this backend serves.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg\-desktop\-portal (1),
.BR xd\-files (1),
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
